WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:03.520
Although Mad Max: Fury Road got rave reviews,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:08.480
Rosie Huntington-Whiteley didn't use her part&nbsp;
as a springboard to advance her acting career.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:11.920
In fact, you might not have seen&nbsp;
Rosie in a hot minute. Here's why.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:17.520
Mad Max: Fury Road was universally praised,&nbsp;
and Rosie Huntington-Whiteley's performance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:22.000
was well received. However, her big screen&nbsp;
debut in Transformers: Dark of the Moon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.960
was panned by critics. In the third installment&nbsp;
of the Transformers franchise, Huntington-Whiteley&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:31.920
replaced Megan Fox as Shia LaBeouf's love&nbsp;
interest. The reviews were so scathing it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:36.880
no wonder she didn't appear in another film for&nbsp;
four years. A review from Total Film remarked,

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:41.200
"[Rosie Huntington-Whiteley was] sucking the&nbsp;
life out of every scene she appeared in."

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:45.520
Every entertainer knows that they can't please&nbsp;
everyone, and the Transformers franchise was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:49.040
never a hit with critics no matter who&nbsp;
was part of the human cast. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:53.040
Huntington-Whiteley said she did her best&nbsp;
to pay attention and learn from the role.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:58.000
Shortly after the release of Mad Max:&nbsp;
Fury Road, Rosie Huntington-Whiteley&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.720
and her boyfriend Jason Statham went public with&nbsp;
the exciting news that they'd gotten engaged.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:08.080
Huntington-Whiteley showed off her sparkly&nbsp;
new rock at the Golden Globes in January 2016.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:12.800
The couple has been together since 2010, and&nbsp;
Huntington-Whiteley says that Statham has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:17.440
much more understanding of her ambitious career&nbsp;
goals than some of her previous boyfriends.

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:18.800
"Are you threatened by him?"

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:25.840
Huntington-Whiteley and Statham are both extremely&nbsp;
passionate about their work, and this connection&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:30.400
only makes their relationship stronger. As&nbsp;
the model and actress told Elle Australia,

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:34.720
"When you're a career-driven person, it works&nbsp;
best when your partner is equally as excited&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:40.000
for you and supportive. And that's what Jason&nbsp;
is. He's my biggest cheerleader and I'm his."

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.720
Although they're both quite busy&nbsp;
with their respective careers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:47.120
they like to have plenty of family time outside&nbsp;
of the spotlight, and Huntington-Whiteley makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:51.360
it a point to keep their relationship fairly&nbsp;
private. They both make an effort to make the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:55.840
most of their time off together, which means not&nbsp;
taking on every project that comes their way.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:02:00.320
Rosie Huntington-Whiteley wears many&nbsp;
professional hats, and by putting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:04.000
acting on the back burner, she was able&nbsp;
to focus on some of her other passions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:09.200
like fashion design. She had already worked on a&nbsp;
lingerie line for British brand Marks and Spencer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:13.600
which turned out to be a massive success, so&nbsp;
it's easy to see why the label Paige chose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:17.520
to partner with her for a collaborative&nbsp;
collection. This was a huge undertaking,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:21.440
but Huntington-Whiteley was happy to&nbsp;
take on the challenge. As she told Elle,

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:26.160
"I've always wanted to be a designer, ever since I&nbsp;
can remember. [...] It's brilliant to come to work&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:30.560
and bring something else to the table beside my&nbsp;
modeling; it's great when people want to listen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:34.960
to you and want you to be a part of something&nbsp;
bigger than just being the face of a brand."

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:38.160
The first collection was&nbsp;
launched in February 2017,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:42.400
and a second was launched in the fall of&nbsp;
2017. It's clear that this is an area where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:46.800
Huntington-Whiteley really excels and feels&nbsp;
comfortable expressing herself creatively.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:51.760
With all the time she's spent acting, modeling,&nbsp;
and working on her other business ventures,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:56.720
it's hard to imagine how Rosie Huntington-Whiteley&nbsp;
could possibly fit anything more into her busy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.720 --> 00:03:01.120
life. Eventually, juggling all of these&nbsp;
commitments was bound to become too much,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:05.120
and as a result, certain projects&nbsp;
inevitably fell by the wayside.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:09.760
Shortly before being cast in Mad Max: Fury&nbsp;
Road, Huntington-Whiteley had been pushing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:15.280
for the presenter spot on the long-running&nbsp;
reality TV series Project Runway All Stars.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:19.600
After getting confirmation that she'd&nbsp;
landed the job, she abruptly backpedaled.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:24.000
Unfortunately for the show, this all went down&nbsp;
mere weeks before filming was slated to begin.

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:29.200
When she was offered the part in Mad Max: Fury&nbsp;
Road, she decided that her role in the film was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:34.080
more important, which unexpectedly left the&nbsp;
cast and crew of Project Runway All Stars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:39.040
in search of a different host. It isn't uncommon&nbsp;
for scheduling conflicts to happen in Hollywood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:43.120
but it still probably didn't do her any favors&nbsp;
with the people behind the scenes at Project&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:48.160
Runway All Stars, and she may have realized that&nbsp;
choosing Hollywood over the fashion industry might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:52.960
not be such a smart career move. Trying to do it&nbsp;
all would just mean spreading herself too thin.

00:03:53.920 --> 00:04:00.080
In June 2017, Rosie Huntington-Whiteley and Jason&nbsp;
Statham welcomed their son, Jack. Like pretty much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:04.960
any doting mom, Huntington-Whiteley never misses&nbsp;
a chance to gush about how much she loves him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:09.440
Although she did take several months off to stay&nbsp;
home with Jack and adjust to being a new mom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:11.520
she says that since she came back to work,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:15.840
she and Statham now try to split their&nbsp;
parenting responsibilities equally.

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:19.040
With Statham's time on film sets,&nbsp;
it would be difficult for both of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:22.800
them to balance time with Jack if&nbsp;
Huntington-Whiteley was acting too.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:26.640
Now, their schedule works out perfectly.&nbsp;
Statham is in charge of Jack in the morning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:30.480
while Huntington-Whiteley takes care of&nbsp;
the nighttime routine and puts him to bed.

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:35.680
"He is very happy to get up at 5 a.m. in&nbsp;
the morning and like do daddy duties."

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:38.240
The couple is adamant that their&nbsp;
son should be raised with plenty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:42.160
of involvement from both parents.&nbsp;
As the model told Harper's Bazaar,

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:45.600
"I think it's so much about raising boys&nbsp;
and girls the same. [...] That's how I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:48.400
was brought up, it's how the&nbsp;
people I love were brought up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:51.120
and they are the values I hope&nbsp;
to instill in my loved ones."

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:55.280
Ask any parent how their life has&nbsp;
changed after they've had a kid,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:59.760
and many will probably tell you that they're not&nbsp;
too keen on staying late at the office anymore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:03.680
as they would rather get home early and have&nbsp;
plenty of time with their family instead.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:08.480
As it turns out, even celebrities struggle to&nbsp;
strike that balance. Rosie Huntington-Whiteley&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:12.080
has been very forthcoming about the&nbsp;
fact that she now considers her son&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:17.360
Jack's needs before she agrees to take any&nbsp;
potential new job. She told Harper's Bazaar,

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:20.160
"The first thing in your mind&nbsp;
before accepting a job is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:23.600
what's right for my family? [...] The&nbsp;
new thing is getting used to having a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:28.400
lot of responsibilities in my personal life and&nbsp;
career. [...] For every woman, it's a juggle."

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:34.160
"We've been so like focused on our work&nbsp;
for so long, and then Jack came along."

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:38.960
In the early days of her career, Rosie&nbsp;
Huntington-Whiteley couldn't afford to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:43.600
picky with her projects, and just like any new&nbsp;
model, she had to be open-minded about the jobs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:49.040
that came her way. But now, she's certainly not&nbsp;
scrounging for work. As one of the most in-demand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:53.520
models in the industry, she can be as choosy&nbsp;
as she wants to be, and she calls the shots.

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:57.440
It seems that 30 was the magic turning&nbsp;
point for Huntington-Whiteley. After&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.440 --> 00:06:02.640
spending nearly 15 years in the industry, she&nbsp;
felt like she had finally gained a solid grasp&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:08.000
on the kinds of jobs that she did or didn't&nbsp;
want to take on. As she told Harper's Bazaar UK,

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:11.520
"I've settled into my life [...] I&nbsp;
know myself and what makes me happy."

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:16.000
Rosie Huntington-Whiteley started&nbsp;
her lifestyle brand, Rose Inc.,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:20.800
while taking her hiatus from modeling to stay home&nbsp;
with son Jack. Huntington-Whiteley says that while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:25.440
acting or modeling, other people are typically&nbsp;
in control of the decisions and final product,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:28.960
but she wanted to pursue a project&nbsp;
where she would have the final say.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:32.720
After years of taking direction from&nbsp;
others, she was ready to make a statement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:36.640
and kick off a whole new phase in&nbsp;
her career. She told Net-a-Porter,

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:40.080
"I just never felt comfortable sitting&nbsp;
back and waiting for other people to make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:44.640
decisions for me. [...] I've always wanted&nbsp;
to be in control of where my life is going."

00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:48.640
Right now, the site features interviews&nbsp;
with models and beauty industry moguls,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:51.840
updates on innovative new&nbsp;
products, and makeup tutorials.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:55.680
It's clear that this is Huntington-Whiteley's&nbsp;
passion, and it's a space where she gets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:58.760
to share all of her interests and&nbsp;
beauty know-how with her friends.

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:04.480
As for why she didn't try to establish herself&nbsp;
as an actress after the success of Mad Max:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:09.680
Fury Road, Rosie Huntington-Whiteley is&nbsp;
a model first and foremost. As of 2018,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:14.400
Huntington-Whiteley was ranked sixth on the Forbes&nbsp;
official rankings of the highest earning models in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:19.040
the world. And those rankings were released while&nbsp;
she was on her maternity break. At this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:23.200
she has the freedom to fully lean into the talents&nbsp;
that have taken her to the top of the ladder,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:27.600
and she knows that she has always had a certain&nbsp;
natural gift for modeling and fashion design.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:31.200
There's a time for trying new things, and&nbsp;
there's a time for embracing your innate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:36.000
talents and just running with them, and that seems&nbsp;
to be where Huntington-Whiteley is at right now.

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:37.760
"It's really about, you know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:41.360
enhancing the things that you love about&nbsp;
yourself and playing on those things."

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:44.800
At the beginning of her modeling&nbsp;
career, Rosie Huntington-Whiteley&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.800 --> 00:07:48.480
said she was simply expected to sit in&nbsp;
front of the camera and look pretty,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:53.120
and she was frustrated with the expectation that&nbsp;
models should stay silent. She says that over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:57.360
the past few years, she's gotten sick of that&nbsp;
feeling, and if she can't give her input and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.360 --> 00:08:02.720
take part in the artistic process, she's just not&nbsp;
interested. Huntington-Whiteley told Net-a-Porter,

00:08:02.720 --> 00:08:06.160
"If shoots aren't a collaborative&nbsp;
process then I'm not really interested,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:09.760
because I don't want to feel like I did&nbsp;
for the first ten years of my career,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:12.080
which is that I was just having stuff done to me."

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:16.160
And as a newcomer to Hollywood,&nbsp;
Huntington-Whiteley probably didn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:20.640
have much sway when it came to how she played&nbsp;
her roles. Perhaps she missed feeling confident&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:24.720
and having a certain level of authority while&nbsp;
having a director in charge of her every move.

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:28.960
Rosie Huntington-Whiteley's dream&nbsp;
was always to become a model,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:32.560
and she made that dream come true at&nbsp;
a young age. But becoming an actress&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.560 --> 00:08:36.240
was never one of her goals. Those&nbsp;
roles happened to fall into her lap,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:40.720
and while she was grateful for the chance to be&nbsp;
part of two franchises that she was a fan of,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:46.080
acting wasn't part of her long-term career plan.&nbsp;
Huntington-Whiteley told The Daily Telegraph,

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:50.000
"They were just incredible opportunities that I've&nbsp;
grasped [...] I think you'll agree when you get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:55.120
to be in a film like Mad Max or Transformers,&nbsp;
you'd be crazy to say no and turn that down."

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:59.120
Huntington-Whiteley has always seen&nbsp;
herself as a model before anything else.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:02.080
She has the incredible career&nbsp;
that she has always envisioned,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:05.520
and while she's glad that she gave&nbsp;
acting a shot, it just wasn't for her.

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:10.560
After spending years in Hollywood, Rosie&nbsp;
Huntington-Whiteley and her family decided&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:15.360
to pack up and move to London in the U.K.&nbsp;
On Instagram, Huntington-Whiteley frequently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:20.320
shares photos from her spacious new home, and she&nbsp;
occasionally posts shots from around the city.

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:24.240
Since Huntington-Whiteley was born and raised&nbsp;
in England, it's safe to say that she wanted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:28.640
to be closer to her family, and perhaps she was&nbsp;
just feeling a little homesick after living so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.640 --> 00:09:33.360
far from her loved ones. While there are plenty of&nbsp;
opportunities for actors in London, it's unlikely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:37.840
that Huntington-Whiteley would want to relocate&nbsp;
there if she intended to return to acting.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:42.480
Of course, actors don't necessarily need to be&nbsp;
based in Los Angeles in order to land roles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:47.360
but it certainly does help. Maybe she'll decide&nbsp;
to come back to California one day, but for now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.360 --> 00:09:51.360
it looks like Huntington-Whiteley and her family&nbsp;
will be staying on the other side of the pond.

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:55.760
Huntington-Whiteley wanted to go&nbsp;
beyond running her own beauty site.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:58.960
She's also passionate about&nbsp;
high-quality cosmetics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:04.000
and she's had the opportunity to collaborate with&nbsp;
several top beauty brands to create new products.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:08.880
In 2020, Huntington-Whiteley became the&nbsp;
first celebrity ambassador for Hourglass&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.880 --> 00:10:12.960
Cosmetics, and she launched a new line of&nbsp;
concealers and lipsticks with the brand.

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:18.080
In January 2021, Huntington-Whiteley worked&nbsp;
with another beauty brand, La Bouche Rouge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:22.240
to release two new shades of lipstick. She&nbsp;
announced that a portion of the proceeds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:27.520
from this particular collection would go to the&nbsp;
non-profit organization Eau Vive Internationale,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:31.440
which provides communities with clean&nbsp;
drinking water. Huntington-Whiteley has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:36.480
spoken of her admiration for the beauty brand&nbsp;
on numerous occasions, and told The Zoe Report,

00:10:36.480 --> 00:10:41.280
"I first came across La Bouche Rouge soon&nbsp;
after it launched in 2017 and instantly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:44.960
fell in love with the sustainability&nbsp;
mission, the clean formulations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.960 --> 00:10:47.760
and how the lipstick cases felt like a keepsake."

00:10:47.760 --> 00:10:50.560
While Huntington-Whiteley&nbsp;
may not be acting right now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.560 --> 00:10:52.960
she's certainly busy enough with other projects.

